<title>ITALY: Italy's Venice sees November CPI at 3.0 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Italy's Venice sees November CPI at 3.0 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>VENICE, Italy 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Venice said its November consumer price index stood at 3.0 percent month-on-month and 0.4 year on year.</p>
<p>In October, the Venice inflation rate was minus 0.2 percent and 3.4 percent respectively.</p>
<p>Venice is one of 10 Italian cities which published inflation data on Thursday and Friday.</p>
<p>The city's CPI has a weighting of 7.89 percent on the national index. The 10 sample cities have a combined weighting of 69.67 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to October 1996):</p>
<p>					  Month/Month	Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		   0.4 (-0.2)	 3.0  (3.4)</p>
<p>    Food			     -0.4 (-0.6)	 2.5  (3.0)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	 0.3  (1.2)	 4.5  (4.7)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges 1.0  (2.5)	 4.9  (3.8)</p>
<p>    Furniture			 0.2  (0.0)	 3.4  (4.8)</p>
<p>    Health services		 0.0  (0.0)	 1.0  (1.1)</p>
<p>    Trasportation		   0.7 (-0.3)	 3.3  (4.1)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture   0.1 (-2.1)	-2.3 (-0.2)</p>
<p>    Education			 4.8  (0.1)	 8.0  (3.0)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	1.2 (-0.5)	 9.0  (7.7)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services    -0.5 (-0.5)	 0.5  (1.2)</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129589</p>
